    "39762eff912edf42ccae7a775a14a67e32aa972c36ff6d82d6d55b86b84157ea": {
      "text": "{\"content\":[{\"text\":\"**Step 1:** Listed the workspace with `ls` — it was empty.\\n\\n**Step 2–3:** Created `notes.md` with the Write tool (two lines) and read it back with Read; both lines were present.\\n\\n**Step 4:** Replaced `scratch` with `fixture` using StrReplace.\\n\\n**Step 5–6:** Glob found `notes.md` among `note*` files; Grep found `fixture` on line 1 of `notes.md`.\\n\\n**Step 7:** Read on `does-not-exist.txt` failed with `File not found`, as expected.\\n\\n**Step 8:** Wrote and ran `count.sh`; output was five lines (`1` through `5`).\\n\\n**Step 9:** The sub-agent reported **11 words** in `notes.md` (per `wc -w` on whitespace-separated tokens).\\n\\n**Summary:** I exercised listing, write, read, search/replace, glob, grep, intentional read failure, shell scripting, and a Task sub-agent — all inside `/Users/ben/projects/temp/cursortest2`. The workspace now has `notes.md` (with “fixture” instead of “scratch”), `count.sh`, and no other files from these steps.\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"id\":\"806616f0-8bff-4afa-b561-609ba3ad59cf\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}"
